.sp 2
.ft AR
LAN Network computers (use Wyse terminals) are available in the
following locations: Hibbs 331 and 341 (M 8a-12,1-2,3:30-7p; T 8a-3:30,
5-8p, W 8a-7p, R 8a-7:30p, F 8a-11a; WP instruction available); GPAB
3307 (M-R 9a-10p; F 9a-4p); Cabell B-8 (M-R 8a-11:45p; F 8a-8:45p; Sa
10a-5:45p; Su 12p-10:45p); Bus 4113 (M-R 8a-11p; F 8a-5p; Sa 9a-5p; Su
1p-11p). These terminals use the PF keys and keypad instead of the usual
WP50 Function keys (see layout on back). Psy labs use F keys and
keypad with some adaptations. 

To begin, type in your \f(HBlogin\f(AR, press return, then type your 
\f(HBpassword\f(AR (these will be on the sheet you pick up from Academic
Computing in the library). If you are not in Cabell, type cabell
when the login first comes up, then enter your computer login.
Note that you will print on the printer in Cabell unless you change
printers by printing from a retrieved file. 

Your first command!
  Type \f(HBx\f(AR to leave menu. You will then be at the cabell% command line.
You have altered your account so that you will now begin with the
command line. If you wish to use e-mail or other features on the menu,
simply type menu at the % in the future.

Type:
  cabell% \f(HB~b8494/setup\f(AR [Please note the tilde]

To WRITE a paper (which you save as a file), SHARE a file with the class, 
GRAB a file from a class folder or
SUBMIT a paper to your professor enter 
.ft ZCMI 
WordPerfect
.ft P
by typing \f(HBwp50\fP at the cabell% prompt.
.ft C

cabell% \f(HBwp50\f(AR

To use SHARE, you  
use a "macro" that tells the computer how to run the program. 
After pressing the PF3 key and then pressing the
2 key on the keypad, you should see the word \fCMacro:\fP at the
bottom left-hand side of the screen.  Type in the word \f(HBshare\fP.
.sp
.ft HB
PF3 KP2
.sp
.ft C
Macro: \f(HBshare\f(AR
.sp
If all is well, you should be looking at the GRAB & SHARE menu.
