.ft CB
                            VCU English Department  
                               Hibbs DEC System                            

                              Class Account Menu                          
                                

                         (s)hare a file with the class             

                         (g)rab a file from the share directory    

                         (t)urn in a file to your instructor

                          e(x)it                        
    
                      Please enter an option from the menu above:
.ps 10
.vs 11
.sp 2
.ft AR
.fi
.in -3i
If you would like to copy a file to a folder where everyone
in the class can read it or turn in to the teacher, then choose \f(HBs\fP to SHARE.  
.BL 2
.LI
Type \f(HBs\f(AR to share. The computer will provide a list of
"folders" that you can share to.  
.LI
(If you are unsure of which folder to use, choose the folder 
called \f(HBClass\f(AR).  Type in the number corresponding to the 
name of the folder you want to
share with, making sure that it is typed the same way that is appears on
the screen.
.LI
Choose the file that you wish to share from your directory.  
A list will be given to you.  Type in the number next to the file name that 
you wish to share.  If a file by the same
name already exists in the folder you have selected, the
computer will ask you to give the file a new name. 
The name of the file in your home directory will remain the same.
.LI
You are finished sharing and will be returned to the GRAB and SHARE menu
where you can share, grab, turn in, or exit (which will return you to
your directory of files).
.LE
.bp
.sp 
If you would like to copy a file from one of the folders to your
account so that you can read it and make comments on it, type \f(HBg\fP
for GRAB.
.BL 3
.LI
Choose a folder by typing in the number next to the folder name.  
.LI
A list of files in the folder is shown.  Type in the number
corresponding to the name of the file that you would like to grab.  
.LI
If a file by the same name already exists in your home directory.  You
will be asked to rename the file your are grabbing.  
.LE
.sp 
To make comments on a file, grab the file and edit it using
.ft ZCMI
WordPerfect.  
.ft AR
Then use the share option to place a copy of the file in  
the \f(HBComments\fP folder.  If you want to see if comments
have been made about your file, use the grab option and choose the
\f(HBComments\fP folder.  Any comments that have been made on your
shared file
be listed and available to grab into your
home directory.
If you are finished using the \f(HBshare\fP macro then choose \f(HBx\fP to
exit the program and return to 
.ft ZCMI
WordPerfect.
.ft AR
To exit after completing work on any files in WordPerfect, type 0
(giving you a blank screen), KP 6 (to exit), N (when asked to save), Y
(when asked if leaving WP50), and type \f(HBlogout\f(AR to finish  your session.

